{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014jWFBuNCgyjBEpYEXw2X7v","type":"tool_result","content":"73-Produces: dated snapshot files in `{book-dir}/sources/` (e.g., `cka-curriculum-2026-04-18.md`) and a `research-manifest.md` listing what was fetched, from what authority, covering which objectives.\n74-\n75-**This is the single most important stage for hallucination prevention.** It fetches authoritative exam curricula and vendor docs, caches them verbatim, and from this point forward **no downstream stage re-fetches from the web**. Every factual claim cited in the draft carries an inline source tag pointing to a cached snapshot. The fact-accuracy audit verifies against the snapshot, not against a second fetch.\n76-\n77-#### 3. Drafting\n78-\n79:Reads: outline, cached sources, knowledge-base shards, skill, style decisions, voice exemplars, branded terms, structural contract.\n80-\n81-Produces: `draft-v1.md` — complete chapter prose with inline source tags and figure anchors.\n82-\n83-Hard rules enforced in prose:\n84-- Source-tag every external factual claim: `[source: slug-YYYY-MM-DD]`.\n85-- Anchor every ASCII diagram: `<!-- FIGURE: chNN-figMM-slug -->`.\n--\n149-Produces: `image-specs.md` for the chapter.\n150-\n151-Sharded per chapter. A book-level aggregator concatenates per-chapter specs into a master index. Every figure-anchor comment in the draft becomes an entry with designer-ready content spec, visual style, and critical-details callouts. Anchor IDs are the join key between draft and spec — never line numbers.\n152-\n153-#### 11. Revision (gated)\n154-\n155:Reads: voiced draft, all diagnostic reports, image specs, cached sources, knowledge-base shards.\n156-\n157-Produces: `draft-v2.md`.\n158-\n159-Applies diagnostic fixes in priority order. Must not regress earlier fixes. Must not invent facts to paper over research gaps.\n160-\n161-Second author gate. After revision, the author confirms the revised draft looks right before final voice pass and integration.\n--\n163-#### 12. Voice Revision (pass 2)\n164-\n165-Same prompt as stage 4. Input is `draft-v2.md`. Output swaps in as the final chapter.\n166-\n167-#### 13. Integration Check (gated)\n168-\n169:Reads: skill, style decisions, draft-v2.md, knowledge-base shards.\n170-\n171-Produces: `integration.md`.\n172-\n173-Last review gate. Cross-chapter terminology consistency, callback accuracy, retrieval-practice alignment, glossary coverage, ethical-guardrails check.\n174-\n175-#### 14. Knowledge Base Update\n--\n180-\n181----\n182-\n183-## Knowledge base — the source of truth\n184-\n185-```\n186:knowledge-base/\n187-├── voice/\n188-│   ├── style-decisions.md          Ratification ledger (author-authored)\n189-│   ├── structural-contract.yaml    Machine-readable layout rules\n190-│   ├── voice-exemplars.md          Prose exemplars tagged by function\n191-│   └── branded-terms.yaml          Canonical brand terminology\n192-├── skill/\n193-│   └── technical-instructional.md  The brand methodology\n194-```\n195-\n196:Brand-level knowledge lives here. Per-book knowledge (exam objectives, glossary, concept shards) lives inside each book's directory under `knowledge-base/`, `sources/`, and `.pipeline-state/`.\n197-\n198-### What replaces alchemy's canon\n199-\n200-Alchemy's canon tracks characters, locations, systems, mysteries — fiction-world source of truth. The cert pipeline's canon-equivalent is split into:\n201-\n202:- **`knowledge-base/voice/`** — brand-wide style & structure authority (shared across books)\n203-- **`{book-dir}/sources/`** — per-book cached authoritative external sources (exam curricula, vendor docs) with dated filenames\n204:- **`{book-dir}/knowledge-base/`** — per-book derived knowledge (glossary, concept shards, objective coverage log)\n205-\n206:The sharding + mention-frequency-filter pattern from alchemy applies to `{book-dir}/knowledge-base/concepts/` when it grows.\n207-\n208-### What was dropped\n209-\n210-| Alchemy construct | Why it doesn't apply |\n211-|---|---|\n212-| Three-axis (genres × modes × intensity) | Discipline is stable per book; pedagogical mode is encoded in per-section difficulty indicators; \"intensity\" in fiction escalates across a series, which has no analogue in certification writing. |\n--\n382-\n383-## Implementation status\n384-\n385-| Capability | Status |\n386-|---|---|\n387-| Skill | **v5.3** |\n388:| Directory structure, knowledge-base seeded | ✓ |\n389-| `style-decisions.md` with identified drift | ✓ (with `[DECIDE]` markers for unresolved questions) |\n390-| `structural-contract.yaml` | ✓ (ambiguity-tolerant pending author decisions) |\n391-| `voice-exemplars.md` | ✓ Provisional (awaiting CAPM freeze) |\n392-| `pipeline/stages.py` (stage graph) | ✓ All 14 stages |\n393-| `pipeline/structural_lint.py` + `--validate-contract` | ✓ |\n394-| `pipeline/config.yaml` with per-book filename patterns | ✓ |\n--\n409-| Model version recorded per stage | ✓ |\n410-| All 14 stage prompts | ✓ first-draft, core 3 reordered for cache |\n411-| Tests (`python tests/run_all.py`) | ✓ 19 tests |\n412-| Book-outline pipeline (5 stages + 5 prompts) | ⚠ Preview |\n413-| Section-wise incremental drafting | ⚠ Preview (standalone tool, not wired into main stage 3 yet) |\n414-| Multi-draft hybrid selection (alchemy's VS) | ✗ Not built — optional future work |\n415:| Full per-book knowledge-base directories | ✗ Empty — populated as chapters run through stage 14 |\n416-\n417-**Immediate next step after reading this:** run `python pipeline/structural_lint.py --all-books --all-chapters`. That's the drift punch list."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4f40c17c-875c-4382-b741-e9203eca6dab","uuid":"fb77e1bd-f3bc-4d48-8025-a9a4dd9a90d7","timestamp":"2026-08-24T04:29:26.821Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"73-Produces: dated snapshot files in `{book-dir}/sources/` (e.g., `cka-curriculum-2026-04-18.md`) and a `research-manifest.md` 